From 54ec958d8addbacaece6003aaa4981cb783f7537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: red-Geck0 <127088086+red-Geck0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:42:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 70/72] feat(hybrid): opt-in Intel XeSS Super Resolution for
 the game's temporal upscale

ASTROHYBRID_XESS=1 replaces Astro Bot's temporal upscale draw (the
pass ASTROHYBRID_DLSS replaces, shader 2936e5eca99d75e7) with XeSS
Super Resolution through the XeSS 3 SDK's Vulkan API, with the same
inputs: SMAA-resolved colour, the game's UV motion vectors (velocity
scale -input size, jittered), the G-buffer depth attachment, the
jitter in input pixels, HDR colour and auto exposure. It runs on any
GPU with DP4a (XMX on Intel Arc) and needs no CUDA address window.

libxess.dll is loaded at run time (next to the game or
ASTROHYBRID_XESS_PATH); the SDK's MIT headers are in 3rdparty/xess.
XeSS's instance and device extensions are enabled where available and
its device features are merged into Kyty's chain (promoted structures
into the Vulkan 1.1-1.3 feature structures, only supported features).
The context is created with the device and builds its pipelines in the
background; each input/output size gets a context initialised on a
worker thread (holding Kyty's queues during xessVKInit), and the
game's own pass runs until it is ready or whenever an input is
missing. ASTROHYBRID_XESS_QUALITY picks a preset (default: the one
whose input range holds the game's size). ASTROHYBRID_DLSS and
ASTROHYBRID_FSR take precedence when set. XeSS frame generation and Xe
Low Latency are D3D12-only in the SDK and are not part of this Vulkan
port. AMD FSR frame generation (ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG) takes its inputs at
the same pass and works together with it.

Tested in game on an Intel Arc B390 with libxess.dll 2.0.2 (its API
and structures match the XeSS 3 headers): 1920x1080 -> 2432x1368,
preset ultra quality plus, every frame, picture correct, frame rate
as with the game's own pass. The unit-test targets that compile every
renderer source have no XeSS include path and get stubs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
